From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] windowscodecs: metadata block writer of encoder frames and the query writer

The IWICMetadataBlockWriter of the JPEG, PNG, TIFF and GIF encoder frames returned
E_NOTIMPL for everything, and IWICMetadataQueryWriter::SetMetadataByName claimed
success while keeping nothing, GetMetadataByName and RemoveMetadataByName were
E_NOTIMPL. Programs that set the orientation, a date or a comment through the
query writer silently lost it.

 - The frames keep the list of writers: GetCount, GetWriterByIndex / GetReaderByIndex,
   AddWriter, SetWriterByIndex, RemoveWriterByIndex (WINCODEC_ERR_VALUEOUTOFRANGE
   past the end), GetEnumerator (a snapshot of the readers), GetContainerFormat and
   InitializeFromBlockReader (a writer made from every reader of the block reader).
 - The query writer reads as the query reader does, and SetMetadataByName walks the
   query ("/app1/ifd/exif/{ushort=34855}"), making the writers on the way (the
   Exif and GPS directories become the values of their pointer tags) before setting
   the item; RemoveMetadataByName removes an item or a whole block.
